Subject: [PATCH 01/10] fix: the client dashboard stops showing fiction as fact
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The home composed seven reads. Three came from the database — project,
journey and current stage. The other four came from src/mocks/hartmann.ts
and rendered with the same typography as the real thing: "needs your
attention", "next delivery", "next meeting" and the learning block.

None of them has an origin in the schema. There is no meetings table and
no metrics tables, and "next delivery" never had a column anywhere — it
is a sibling of the project scope that phase 6 removed.

Worse, the attention CTA pointed at a hard-coded route with a project id
that stopped existing in phase 6, so the most important call to action in
the product answered with a 404.

The four blocks are gone. A source-code guard reads the home and fails if
any of them returns, because a mock comes back through a bad revert long
before anyone notices it on screen.

The attention block returns later in this phase, derived from real data.

